@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ocar-tests-fixtures`
IMPORT `ocar-04-05-06-duties`
IMPORT `ocar-claim`

-- TESTS for what each party must do, and by when: Articles 2-8 and 10, the personal data
-- clause, and the choice of version. Expected values are worked by hand from the source (the
-- working is in the comment beside each), before the assertion was run.
--
-- DAYS. The tests count working days on `the test calendar` (ocar-tests-fixtures.l4): the
-- weekends of June to October 2026 and no holiday. That is a test value, not a claim about
-- which days are working days in Vietnam. Wednesday 10 June 2026 is the usual day 0.

§ `Tests — duties, deadlines and termination`

§§ `Counting working days`

-- 5 working days from Wednesday 10 June (the day itself not counted, fork F7): 11, 12, 15, 16,
-- 17 June. 7 calendar days.
#ASSERT `the end of` 5 `working days counted from` (YMD 2026 6 10) `skipping` `the test calendar` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 17
#ASSERT `the calendar days in` 5 `working days counted from` (YMD 2026 6 10) `skipping` `the test calendar` EQUALS 7
-- 15 working days: to Wednesday 1 July (21 calendar days); 30: to Wednesday 22 July (42).
#ASSERT `the calendar days in` 15 `working days counted from` (YMD 2026 6 10) `skipping` `the test calendar` EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `the calendar days in` 30 `working days counted from` (YMD 2026 6 10) `skipping` `the test calendar` EQUALS 42

§§ `The version of the rules`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The policy`
`the policy concluded on` d MEANS
    `a 2026 policy on` `the private car` `, concluded on` d `, insured for` 600_000_000 `, market value` (JUST 600_000_000) `, with` EMPTY

-- src:5-7: Decision 124/2019 of 31/12/2019; Decision 17/2022 of 28/03/2022 (forks F1, F2).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the version of the rules governing` (`the policy concluded on` (YMD 2019 12 30)) BECAUSE "no version of the rules before Decision 124/2019 of 31/12/2019 is in the document"
#ASSERT `the version of the rules governing` (`the policy concluded on` (YMD 2019 12 31)) EQUALS `the rules as made by Decision 124/2019`
#ASSERT `the version of the rules governing` (`the policy concluded on` (YMD 2022 3 27)) EQUALS `the rules as made by Decision 124/2019`
#ASSERT `the version of the rules governing` (`the policy concluded on` (YMD 2022 3 28)) EQUALS `the rules as amended by the supplementary clauses of Decision 17/2022`

§§ `Article 2.3 and Article 3 — transfer and termination`

`the policy with half the premium paid by 15 January` MEANS `the plain policy with deductible` NOTHING `, reduction level` NOTHING `, premium paid` 6_000_000 `, owing allowed` FALSE `, other policies` EMPTY

-- 3.1.1, src:162-166: unpaid by 15 January, no deferral: ends that day. Paid in full: no end.
#ASSERT `3.1.1 — the date the contract terminates for late premium` `the policy with half the premium paid by 15 January` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `3.1.1 — the date the contract terminates for late premium` `the plain policy` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 3.1.2-3.1.3, src:167-177: owed to 15 January: 12,000,000 x 15/365 (1 to 15 January, of 365
-- days); refund 70% of the excess of the 6,000,000 paid, less a 50,000 cost of refunding
-- (src:198-201); nothing if an insured event has happened.
#ASSERT `3.1.2 — the premium owed up to termination` `the policy with half the premium paid by 15 January` `on` (YMD 2026 1 15) EQUALS (12_000_000 TIMES 15) DIVIDED BY 365
#ASSERT `3.1.3 — the refund after termination for late premium` `the policy with half the premium paid by 15 January` `,` FALSE `,` 50_000 EQUALS JUST ((70% TIMES (6_000_000 MINUS ((12_000_000 TIMES 15) DIVIDED BY 365))) MINUS 50_000)
#ASSERT `3.1.3 — the refund after termination for late premium` `the policy with half the premium paid by 15 January` `,` TRUE `,` 50_000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- 3.2.2, src:184-190: the Policyholder ends it on 1 July; 183 of 365 days remain (2 July to 31
-- December): 70% of 12,000,000 x 183/365; nothing after an insured event.
#ASSERT `3.2.2 — the refund on the Policyholder's termination` `the plain policy` `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` FALSE `,` 0 EQUALS (8_400_000 TIMES 183) DIVIDED BY 365
#ASSERT `3.2.2 — the refund on the Policyholder's termination` `the plain policy` `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` TRUE `,` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `3.2.2 — the refund on the Policyholder's termination` `the policy with half the premium paid by 15 January` `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` FALSE `,` 0 BECAUSE "3.2.2 does not say how the refund is computed when the premium has not been paid in full"
-- 3.2.3, src:193-197: the Insurer ends it on 1 July: 100% of 12,000,000 x 183/365.
#ASSERT `3.2.3 — the refund on the Insurer's termination` `the plain policy` `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS (12_000_000 TIMES 183) DIVIDED BY 365
-- 2.3, src:139-148: a lawful transfer passes the benefits unless the Policyholder asks for the
-- refund instead, which is 3.2.2's (fork F12).
#ASSERT `2.3 — the benefits pass to the transferee` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `2.3 — the benefits pass to the transferee` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `2.3 — the refund on a transfer without the benefits` `the plain policy` `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` FALSE `,` 0 EQUALS (8_400_000 TIMES 183) DIVIDED BY 365
-- 3.2.1, src:179-183: notice on Monday 5 October; 5 working days later is Monday 12 October.
#ASSERT `3.2.1 — the earliest date a termination noticed on` (YMD 2026 10 5) `may take effect, skipping` `the test calendar` EQUALS YMD 2026 10 12
#ASSERT `3.2.2 — the date the contract ends on the Policyholder's notice received on` (YMD 2026 10 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 5

-- The refund duties as traces: 3.2.2 within 15 days.
#TRACE `3.2.2 — the Insurer's duty to refund` 1_000_000 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insurer` DOES `refund the premium` 1_000_000 AT 15
#TRACE `3.2.2 — the Insurer's duty to refund` 1_000_000 AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 16)
-- 3.1.3 within 5 working days of termination on 10 June: by day 7.
#TRACE `3.1.3 — the Insurer's duty to refund` 1_000_000 `after termination on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `skipping` `the test calendar` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insurer` DOES `refund the premium` 1_000_000 AT 7
#TRACE `3.1.3 — the Insurer's duty to refund` 1_000_000 `after termination on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `skipping` `the test calendar` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)

§§ `Article 4 — the Insurer's duty to pay, and its period`

-- src:238-242: 15 working days of a complete file (to day 21), 30 where it must verify (day 42).
#ASSERT `4.2 — the working days to pay` FALSE EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `4.2 — the working days to pay` TRUE EQUALS 30
#TRACE `4.2 — the Insurer's duty to pay` 9_500_000 `, the file complete on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `, verification needed:` FALSE `, skipping` `the test calendar` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insurer` DOES `pay the indemnity` 9_500_000 AT 21
#TRACE `4.2 — the Insurer's duty to pay` 9_500_000 `, the file complete on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `, verification needed:` FALSE `, skipping` `the test calendar` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 22)
#TRACE `4.2 — the Insurer's duty to pay` 9_500_000 `, the file complete on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `, verification needed:` TRUE `, skipping` `the test calendar` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insurer` DOES `pay the indemnity` 9_500_000 AT 42
-- src:243-245: where the Insurer cannot verify, the file counts as complete only on the
-- authority's conclusion; with none, never.
#ASSERT `4.2 — the date the file counts as complete` TRUE (YMD 2026 6 10) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)
#ASSERT `4.2 — the date the file counts as complete` FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.2 — the date the file counts as complete` FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 9 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 9 1)
-- src:248-252: after 90 days without the authority's result, the Insurer verifies and may settle.
#ASSERT `4.2 — the Insurer verifies by itself and may consider settling` 91 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `4.2 — the Insurer verifies by itself and may consider settling` 90 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `4.2 — the Insurer verifies by itself and may consider settling` 91 TRUE

