§§ `Article 7 — who pays for the assessment`

-- src:400-401: the Insurer pays its own. src:410-424: the independent conclusion the same as the
-- Insurer's: the Policyholder pays; different, by even one dong: the Insurer pays.
#ASSERT `7 — the party who pays for the Insurer's assessment` EQUALS `the Insurer`
#ASSERT `7 — the party who pays for the independent assessment and the court fees` "collision" 10_000_000 "collision" 10_000_000 EQUALS `the Policyholder`
#ASSERT `7 — the party who pays for the independent assessment and the court fees` "collision" 10_000_000 "collision" 10_000_001 EQUALS `the Insurer`
#ASSERT `7 — the party who pays for the independent assessment and the court fees` "collision" 10_000_000 "fire" 10_000_000 EQUALS `the Insurer`

§§ `Article 8 — the claim file`

`an accident the police dealt with, a third party liable` MEANS `The facts the claim file depends on` WITH
    `the vehicle was sold, transferred, given or lent under an authority` IS FALSE
    `the vehicle runs under a temporary permit or is in its first registration` IS FALSE
    `towing was hired`                                       IS FALSE
    `repaired outside the Insurer's guarantee network`       IS FALSE
    `a valuation is needed`                                  IS FALSE
    `the whole vehicle was stolen, robbed or disappeared`    IS FALSE
    `costs were incurred to limit the loss or on the Insurer's instructions` IS FALSE
    `there was a mediation`                                  IS FALSE
    `there is a court judgment or decision`                  IS FALSE
    `a third party is liable`                                IS TRUE
    `the police dealt with the accident`                     IS TRUE
    `there are other relevant papers`                        IS FALSE
    `there is a decision to prosecute`                       IS FALSE
    `there is a decision to suspend`                         IS FALSE
    `papers were lost with the vehicle`                      IS FALSE
-- src:430-488: the documents the text makes applicable, in its order.
#ASSERT `8 — the documents the claim file may include, for` `an accident the police dealt with, a third party liable` EQUALS LIST `notice of the accident and claim, on the Insurer's form`, `the certificate or the contract, and other written agreements`, `the vehicle registration, and the Driver's licence valid at the time of the loss`, `a valid inspection certificate, or an equivalent paper`, `papers transferring the claim against the third party to the Insurer`, `copies of the police file on the accident`, `papers on the liability of a third party`, `the assessment report the parties agreed`

§§ `Article 10 — time limits`

-- src:533-535: one year from the event; leap day to 28 February; plus days of excused delay.
#ASSERT `10 — the last day to claim, for an event on` (YMD 2025 2 28) `with` 0 `days of delay` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `10 — the last day to claim, for an event on` (YMD 2024 2 29) `with` 0 `days of delay` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `10 — the last day to claim, for an event on` (YMD 2025 2 28) `with` 10 `days of delay` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
-- src:536-542: 90 days from receiving the notice: 10 June to 8 September; 5 days lost: 13 September.
#ASSERT `10 — the last day to complain, notice received on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 0 `days lost` EQUALS YMD 2026 9 8
#ASSERT `10 — the last day to complain, notice received on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `with` 5 `days lost` EQUALS YMD 2026 9 13
-- src:543-545: three years from the dispute.
#ASSERT `10 — the last day to sue, the dispute having arisen on` (YMD 2026 6 10) EQUALS YMD 2029 6 10

§§ `The personal data clause`

-- src:1237-1241: no consent to the whole clause: no contract, so no cover.
`the policy without data consent` MEANS `The policy` WITH
    `vehicle`                                                         IS `the private car`
    `date the contract was concluded`                                 IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `start of the insurance period`                                   IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `last day of the insurance period`                                IS YMD 2026 12 31
    `sum insured`                                                     IS 600_000_000
    `market value when insured`                                       IS JUST 600_000_000
    `price of the vehicle new (100%)`                                 IS 800_000_000
    `minimum remaining-quality rate in the import customs declaration` IS NOTHING
    `deductible stated in the contract`                               IS NOTHING
    `reduction level stated in the contract`                          IS NOTHING
    `premium`                                                         IS 12_000_000
    `premium paid`                                                    IS 12_000_000
    `last day for paying the premium`                                 IS YMD 2026 1 15
    `the Insurer agreed that the premium may be owed`                 IS FALSE
    `supplementary clauses`                                           IS EMPTY
    `other policies on the vehicle`                                   IS EMPTY
    `the personal data clause is part of the contract`                IS TRUE
    `the data subject agreed to the whole personal data clause`       IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `data clause 9 — the contract stands, on` `the policy without data consent`
#ASSERT `data clause 9 — the contract stands, on` `the plain policy`
#ASSERT `the amount payable on the claim, with no reduction under Article 16` (`a claim on` `the policy without data consent` `for` `the plain collision`) EQUALS 0
-- src:1242-1249: exercising a right under clause 4, 5, 6 or 8 of Article 9 of Decree 13/2023
-- ends the contract as the Policyholder's own termination: 3.2.2's 70%, or nothing after an
-- insured event. Clause 3 does not.
#ASSERT `data clause 10 — the contract ends, on` `the plain policy` `, when a right is exercised under clause` 4
#ASSERT NOT `data clause 10 — the contract ends, on` `the plain policy` `, when a right is exercised under clause` 3
#ASSERT `data clause 10 — the refund, on` `the plain policy` `, a right exercised under clause` 5 `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` FALSE `,` 0 EQUALS JUST ((8_400_000 TIMES 183) DIVIDED BY 365)
#ASSERT `data clause 10 — the refund, on` `the plain policy` `, a right exercised under clause` 5 `on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `,` TRUE `,` 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- src:1233-1236: the clause cites Decree 13/2023 of 17/04/2023; an earlier contract that says
-- it carries the clause is declined (fork F3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `the personal data clause applies to` (`the policy concluded on` (YMD 2023 4 16)) BECAUSE "the personal data clause cites Decree 13/2023 of 17/04/2023 and cannot be part of an earlier contract"
#ASSERT `the personal data clause applies to` (`the policy concluded on` (YMD 2023 4 17))
-- src:1230-1232: processing stops within 72 hours of a request to delete (clock in hours).
#TRACE `data clause 7(b) — the Insurer's duty to stop processing within 72 hours of a request to delete` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Insurer` DOES `stop processing the personal data` AT 72
#TRACE `data clause 7(b) — the Insurer's duty to stop processing within 72 hours of a request to delete` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 73)
